                                "sense_id": "48bac5d2-af0d-3efe-a2a4-4ff66a20e6de",
                                "text": "The next day was to take us to Anár, over a desert of twelve farsakhs, and it was here we might expect the robbers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c6eae91f-37ae-43ef-adc1-13cb078350c9",
                                "sense_id": "48bac5d2-af0d-3efe-a2a4-4ff66a20e6de",
                                "text": "The old authors considered Demâvend the highest mountain in the world, and estimated its height at four to five farsaks"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "039730c1-2d15-4263-92e6-21bcae94a489",
                                "sense_id": "48bac5d2-af0d-3efe-a2a4-4ff66a20e6de",
                                "text": "From Rai to Damghan, 80 farsakhs; from Damghan to Nishapur, 80; total from Rai to Nishapur, 160 farsakhs."
                            }
                        ]
